methods.explanation:
To add the fractions, give them the common denominator \(6x\), which is nonzero because \(x\ne0\). Then
\[
\begin{aligned}
\frac1x+\frac1{2x}+\frac1{3x}
&=\frac6{6x}+\frac3{6x}+\frac2{6x}\\
&=\frac{6+3+2}{6x}\\
&=\frac{11}{6x}.
\end{aligned}
\]
The answer is \(\frac{11}{6x}\), choice \(\mathrm{D}\).
